    ("How do you calculate weighted average in Excel?", "=SUMPRODUCT(Values, Weights) / SUM(Weights)."),
    ("What does the TRANSPOSE function do in Excel?", "It flips the orientation of a range from vertical to horizontal or vice versa."),
    ("What is the difference between AND and OR functions in Excel?", "AND returns TRUE only if all conditions are TRUE; OR returns TRUE if at least one condition is TRUE."),
    ("How do you nest an IF formula with multiple conditions in modern Excel?", "Use the IFS function: =IFS(A2 >= 90, 'A', A2 >= 80, 'B', TRUE, 'C')."),
    ("What does the EXACT function do in Excel?", "It compares two text strings and returns TRUE only if they are identical, including case sensitivity."),
    ("How do you count cells containing specific text in Excel?", "=COUNTIF(Range, '*text*') using asterisks as wildcards for partial matching."),
    ("What do question marks (?) and asterisks (*) represent in Excel criteria?", "A question mark matches any single character; an asterisk matches any sequence of characters."),
    ("What is an Excel Macro?", "A recorded sequence of user actions or VBA code executed on demand to automate repetitive tasks."),
    ("What is the standard file extension for an Excel workbook containing macros?", ".xlsm (Excel Macro-Enabled Workbook); standard .xlsx files cannot store executable VBA code."),
    ("How do you create a dynamic named range in Excel?", "Use Formulas -> Name Manager and define the reference using dynamic array functions or OFFSET/COUNTA."),
    ("What does the FORMULATEXT function do in Excel?", "It returns the formula of a referenced cell as a text string, useful for documentation and audit reviews."),
    ("How do you find the second largest value in a range in Excel?", "=LARGE(Range, 2). To find the smallest, use =SMALL(Range, 2)."),
